Correction: the transcription above is incomplete and does not follow the required format. The full verse should be transcribed as printed:

<page type="text">
  <layout>One page: running head at top; title and number above an engraved frame (no text inside); verse of four lines below the frame; the word "Homo" at lower right.</layout>
  <running_head>THEOD. BEZÆ</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <head level="1">Cœlum tonans simul & plucens.</head>
    <head level="3">XXXXI.</head>
    <p>Eu rutilis idem qui diſilit ignibus æther,</p>
    <l>Fœcundus grauido pectore fundit aquas:</l>
    <l>Vita fide sic Chriſtus erit tibi Vera receptus,</l>
    <l>Spretus at hic idem mors tibi Chriſtus erit.</l>
    <p>Homo</p>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The engraved frame holds no text. The large initial C of the first line is printed as an ornamental letter and is joined to "Eu" in the first line; the reading "Ceu" is likely. The title line reads "Cœlum tonans simul & pluens" in the print; "plucens" is uncertain. Words "Vera" and "Spretus" are as printed.</notes>
</page>